{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1230937","formula":"C₁₀H₁₈ClN₃O₂","hill":"C10H18ClN3O2","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":18.0,"N":3.0,"O":2.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Semustine","ru":"Семустин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Semustine (1-(2-chloroethyl)-3-(trans-4-methylcyclohexyl)-1-nitrosourea, MeCCNU) is an alkylating nitrosourea compound used in chemotherapy treatment of various types of tumours. Due to its lipophilic property, semustine can cross the blood-brain barrier for the chemotherapy of brain tumours, where it interferes with DNA replication in the rapidly-dividing tumour cells. Semustine, just as lomustine, is administered orally.","ru":"Семустин — цитостатический противоопухолевый химиотерапевтический лекарственный препарат из группы производных нитрозомочевины. Семустин химически очень близок к ломустину и отличается от него только одной дополнительной метильной группой. Он был изъят с рынка в связи с обнаружением у него канцерогенных свойств."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":5198,"mass":247.72,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1CCC(CC1)NC(=O)N(CCCl)N=O","inchikey":"FVLVBPDQNARYJU-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(2-chloroethyl)-3-(4-methylcyclohexyl)-1-nitrosourea","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5198","atoms":34,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":5.837,"y":0.595,"z":0.014,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.191,"y":1.837,"z":-0.364,"el":"O"},{"x":2.472,"y":-2.569,"z":-0.025,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.329,"y":0.24,"z":0.289,"el":"N"},{"x":1.901,"y":-0.364,"z":-0.215,"el":"N"},{"x":1.535,"y":-1.774,"z":0.103,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.985,"y":-0.242,"z":-0.136,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.425,"y":1.169,"z":0.442,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.232,"y":-0.473,"z":1.18,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.017,"y":0.145,"z":-1.261,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.372,"y":0.733,"z":1.563,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.169,"y":1.36,"z":-0.883,"el":"C"},{"x